Verse 1:
[G]Blessed Jesus, [Am]at Thy word,
[Em/B]We [Bm]are [G]gathered [D7/C]all to [D]hear [D7/C]Thee;
[G]Let our [Am]hearts and [G]souls [Am]be stirred,
[Em/B]Now [Bm]to seek [G]and love [D7/C]and [G/D]fear [D]Thee.
[Em/B]By [Bm]Thy [D/A]teachings sweet [Em/B]and [Am]holy,
[G]Drawn [Em]from earth [D7/C]to [G]love [C]Thee [G]sole [D7/C]ly.

Verse 2:
[G]All our [Am]knowledge, [G]sense, [Am]and sight,
[Em/B]Lie [Bm]in [G]deepest [D7/C]darkness [D]shrouded;
[G]Till Thy [Am]Spirit [G]breaks [Am]our night,
[Em/B]With [Bm]His beams [G]of truth [D7/C]unclouded.
[Em/B]He [Bm]alone [C/G]to [D/A]God [Em/B]canst [Am]win [D/A]us,
[G]He [Em]who works [G]all [C]good within [D7/C]us.

Verse 3:
[G]Glorious [Am]Lord, Thy [G]self [Am]impart!
[Em/B]Light [Bm]of [G]light, from [D7/C]God proceeding.
[G]Open [Am]Thou our [G]ears [Am]and heart
[Em/B]Help [Bm]us, by [G]Thy Spirit's pleading.
[Em/B]Hear [Bm]the [D/A]cry [C/G]Thy [D/A]people [Am]raises!
[G]Hear, [Em]and bless [G]our [C]prayer and [Am/E]praises!
